ushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 29%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $109 to $256 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/E 40.3 vs 22.1, EV/EBITDA 17.0 vs 12.9 and P/FCF 36.4 vs 21.8 (sector median).","The EBIT multiple is close to its own 10-year median (-1%).","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 2.7% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 3.1% (vs the 8% bar).","The 25 covering analysts target $207 on average, 15% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 7% earns above the cost of capital of 7.0%, but the 0pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.51).","It converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.24x.","ROE of 13% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.6x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.8% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 3.0x net debt to EBITDA ($46.0M of cash against $8.8B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 5.1x.","The current ratio of 0.62 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","Goodwill makes up 40% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 9.5% over 3 years, 11.7% over 5 years and 17.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 20%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 8.8% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.8% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 9%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.0x, 12.5% of sales), a maintenance pace."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.3%), and institutions hold 91%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (16 sales, net $6.7M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.9% (1.1% in buybacks and 0.9% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 0.8% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 15 consecutive years, raising it 10.8% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 24,214 employees, each generates about $391K of revenue, in line with the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 12.4% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $51K of free cash flow per employee.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $4.5M (11x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":59,"head":"Watch: composite 43, above the 39 line, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $140.","pros":["Composite 43, above the 39 line (gates 10/25)","FCF margin 13.0%","Revenue grew 11.7%/yr over 5y","Altman Z in the safe zone","25 analysts' mean target $207 (+15%)"],"cons":["Trades 9% above fair value of $165","P/E 40.3x vs sector 22.1x","EV/EBITDA 17.0x vs sector 12.9x","P/FCF 36.4x vs sector 21.8x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":140.25,"vc":{"base":165.01,"base_src":"dcf","bear":108.7,"bull":256.06,"alt_median":39.45,"n_alt":3,"gap":3.1821,"dispersion":0.2864,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 318% above the other models' median ($39.45)"]},"med":{"pe":22.1377,"ev_ebitda":12.904,"pfcf":21.8001,"pb":2.7623,"roic":0.0997,"gross_margin":0.2864,"fcf_margin":0.0677,"div_yield":0.0151}},"mc_quantiles":[76.93,95.75,108.7,116.98,127.33,134.91,140.2,147.28,153.69,159.93,167.45,175.47,181.69,188.59,198.96,208.77,218.67,234.01,256.06,286.08,361.81],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.529,"discount_rate":0.402,"terminal_growth":0.03,"exit_multiple":0.039},"ticker":"WCN","date":"2026-11-20"}